    "text": "Hi team, could I get some \u003c#C081MV728N7\u003e  with a data type replication issue?\n\nWe have an `INT` column in our MariaDB source, and we expect it to be replicated as `INT` in the destination Parquet files on S3. However, OLake is consistently writing the column as `BIGINT`/`INT64` in the Parquet schema.\n\n*Source:* MariaDB (MySQL) — `INT(11)`\n*Destination:* S3 — Parquet\n\nWe were initially running OLake *v0.6.4*, and I suspected this might be version-specific. I also tested the same table with *v0.10.0*, but the column is still being written as `BIGINT`/`INT64`.\n\nThis isn't blocking us immediately, but we'd like to understand the root cause before proceeding further, especially since the expected source-to-destination data type mapping is important for our downstream analytical workloads.\n\nCould someone please help us understand why `INT(11)` is being mapped to `BIGINT`/`INT64` in the Parquet output? Is there any configuration or recommended approach to preserve the `INT` data type?\n\nAny guidance or pointers to the relevant code/documentation would be greatly appreciated. Thanks!",
    "ts": "1789128697.791379",
